+# Atomic native destination registration
+
+`rotation_native_register` records a verified native restoration under the existing source intent. It accepts the exact native ACK request plus `target`: enrollment, runtime_id, rollout_path, binding_revision, and the logical ledger thread_id.
+
+The host must first reread private native journals and verify the exact currently attached destination and retained process/worker incarnation. Submitted JSON is descriptive evidence, not lifecycle authority. Registration does not close, restore, release, or acknowledge a native thread.
+
+TaskLedger publishes source epoch registration and destination session/provenance in one WAL batch before exposing either. Existing generic destination rows are refused, including otherwise matching rows. Exact repeats return the durable registration without writing; conflicting provenance is refused. rotation_status exposes registration only once present. Source and destination logical identity are fenced until ACK; session_bind cannot manufacture native_registration metadata.
+
+An expired preparation lease does not prevent recording restoration against a durable pending intent. The native receipt, claim/token/host claim, request digest, current logical task, exact target runtime/rollout and same process/worker enrollment must match. First ACK after registration must match its receipt and target provenance. Existing historical ACK behavior remains compatible.
+
+Lost replies are reconciled with rotation_status(session_id, epoch) and session_get(target): both carry the same registration record. A missing or conflicting destination never gets silently repaired. The full host driver, durable registration/ACK phases and native/host fence retirement remain separate work.
